{"file":"command.go","line":1241,"severity":"high","confidence_score":85,"text":"mergePersistentFlags and the new LocalFlags no longer fold in the global pflag.CommandLine flags for the root command. The old code did this. Flags added with `pflag.CommandLine.AddGoFlagSet(...)` (glog, for example) are no longer parsed or listed, so passing `--v=2` now fails with 'unknown flag'."},
{"file":"command.go","line":1103,"severity":"medium","confidence_score":80,"text":"addToLocal skips any flag whose name is in parentsPflags. A child that defines its own local or persistent flag with the same name as a parent's persistent flag (for example `--config`) is dropped from LocalFlags. The same name also appears in InheritedFlags, so help and usage show the parent's flag and omit the child's."},
{"file":"command.go","line":1120,"severity":"medium","confidence_score":80,"text":"iflags, lflags and parentsPflags are cached and only ever added to, never rebuilt. If a flag is added to a parent after the first InheritedFlags or LocalFlags call, or a flag is removed or replaced, the child keeps returning stale entries. Previously a fresh FlagSet was built on every call."}
